1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,159
This is the Quest Log, on Helm,

2
00:00:02,609 --> 00:00:05,662
and that quest, Close Inspection, is mine.

3
00:00:06,562 --> 00:00:09,336
Fifteen lines in a text file put it there.

4
00:00:10,236 --> 00:00:13,773
And in the next few minutes, you'll write your own first quest,

5
00:00:14,223 --> 00:00:16,026
and you won't write any code to do it.

6
00:00:17,826 --> 00:00:19,357
This is your fact sheet.

7
00:00:20,257 --> 00:00:21,895
Two hashes make a section,

8
00:00:22,345 --> 00:00:24,353
and this section is Quests,

9
00:00:24,803 --> 00:00:28,638
so everything under it is a quest, until the next section starts.

10
00:00:29,538 --> 00:00:33,818
Right now it holds one story, First Contact, in two steps.

11
00:00:34,718 --> 00:00:36,046
We're going to leave that alone,

12
00:00:36,496 --> 00:00:38,134
and add one of our own underneath it.

13
00:00:39,934 --> 00:00:41,434
Here's where the crew will read it.

14
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:44,794
On the left is the Quest Log's list,

15
00:00:45,244 --> 00:00:48,118
and on the right, for the quest that's selected,

16
00:00:48,568 --> 00:00:52,140
its state, its reward, its order, and its briefing.

17
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:55,903
Every one of those is a line I'm about to type.

18
00:00:57,703 --> 00:01:01,157
I start with three hashes, which makes this a quest of its own.

19
00:01:02,057 --> 00:01:05,645
Then the name, which is what the crew sees in that list,

20
00:01:06,095 --> 00:01:08,060
and a key, which they never see.

21
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,543
Then I open the fence.

22
00:01:12,343 --> 00:01:15,211
Shared means it's one quest for the whole crew.

23
00:01:16,111 --> 00:01:19,879
Starts when, at once, means it's in the Quest Log

24
00:01:20,329 --> 00:01:22,354
as soon as the game starts.

25
00:01:23,254 --> 00:01:26,137
The objective is the order, in one sentence,

26
00:01:26,587 --> 00:01:29,752
and the crew reads it on the right, above the description.

27
00:01:30,652 --> 00:01:33,430
Done when is the one we'll come back to.

28
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:37,932
Then comes the reward, which is the Reward line on the right,

29
00:01:38,382 --> 00:01:39,596
and I close the fence.

30
00:01:41,396 --> 00:01:43,045
And last comes the description,

31
00:01:43,495 --> 00:01:45,478
which the crew reads under the order.

32
00:01:46,378 --> 00:01:48,398
It's a short page, so I write it like one.

33
00:01:49,298 --> 00:01:51,041
First a line of story,

34
00:01:51,491 --> 00:01:54,675
then a blank line, and what DS 1 knows so far.

35
00:01:55,575 --> 00:01:59,748
Then a heading, which is two hashes and a space, with no brackets,

36
00:02:00,198 --> 00:02:03,071
so it's part of the description, and not a record.

37
00:02:03,971 --> 00:02:05,738
And last, what's at stake.

38
00:02:07,538 --> 00:02:09,787
This is the line that matters most.

39
00:02:10,687 --> 00:02:15,289
It's a verb, then a role, then a number, in that order.

40
00:02:17,089 --> 00:02:18,627
Reach means get close,

41
00:02:19,077 --> 00:02:21,246
and five hundred is how close.

42
00:02:22,146 --> 00:02:23,542
And derelict is a role,

43
00:02:23,992 --> 00:02:25,394
which you met last time.

44
00:02:26,294 --> 00:02:27,433
Here's the hulk's list:

45
00:02:27,883 --> 00:02:30,648
its side, and then the two roles it wears.

46
00:02:31,548 --> 00:02:35,887
The promise is the same as it was for the sentence on Science's Intel tab:

47
00:02:36,337 --> 00:02:38,128
something has to wear the word.

48
00:02:39,928 --> 00:02:41,934
What's new here is the verb.

49
00:02:42,834 --> 00:02:45,391
Last time, a step waited for a signal,

50
00:02:45,841 --> 00:02:47,883
and this file had to say it.

51
00:02:48,783 --> 00:02:50,620
But reach is built in,

52
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:53,691
so the game does the watching itself.

53
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:56,538
And that's why there's nothing to change in here.

54
00:02:58,338 --> 00:03:01,578
Here are two slips that lint catches.

55
00:03:02,478 --> 00:03:06,091
The word When, on its own, means when the quest starts,

56
00:03:06,541 --> 00:03:09,148
so nothing ever finishes this quest,

57
00:03:09,598 --> 00:03:11,565
and lint says exactly that.

58
00:03:12,465 --> 00:03:14,202
Then there's a role spelled wrong:

59
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:17,140
nothing wears it, and lint says that too.

60
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:20,490
Now here's one it doesn't catch.

61
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:25,316
If I take out the line that says Starts when, at once,

62
00:03:25,766 --> 00:03:27,211
lint still says clean,

63
00:03:27,661 --> 00:03:29,650
but the quest is only on offer.

64
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:33,155
So here's where my quest went instead.

65
00:03:34,055 --> 00:03:35,823
It isn't in the Quest Log at all.

66
00:03:36,273 --> 00:03:39,224
It's on the ePADD's other list, Available Quests,

67
00:03:39,674 --> 00:03:42,552
and it waits there until someone on Comms accepts it.

68
00:03:44,352 --> 00:03:46,206
The page has a table of these,

69
00:03:46,656 --> 00:03:48,773
and the ones to remember are these:

70
00:03:49,223 --> 00:03:52,052
the number goes last, and nothing goes after it,

71
00:03:52,502 --> 00:03:54,497
and count your hashes.

72
00:03:56,297 --> 00:03:59,653
Now I put everything back the way it was, and run lint.

73
00:04:00,553 --> 00:04:03,997
And it's clean, with no errors and no warnings.

74
00:04:05,797 --> 00:04:08,809
Here's the Quest Log, and here's mine in the list.

75
00:04:09,709 --> 00:04:13,294
On the right are its state, its reward and my order.

76
00:04:14,194 --> 00:04:15,849
Under them is my description,

77
00:04:16,299 --> 00:04:18,659
three short paragraphs with a heading,

78
00:04:19,109 --> 00:04:21,998
and a gap wherever I left a blank line.

79
00:04:22,898 --> 00:04:24,661
So now we fly out to the hulk.

80
00:04:26,461 --> 00:04:29,241
At two thousand, Find the Derelict is done.

81
00:04:30,141 --> 00:04:32,977
But that's last lecture's signal, and not my quest,

82
00:04:33,427 --> 00:04:34,662
so mine hasn't moved.

83
00:04:36,462 --> 00:04:38,685
Then, once we're inside five hundred,

84
00:04:39,135 --> 00:04:42,838
Helm shows a green line: Quest complete, Close Inspection.

85
00:04:43,738 --> 00:04:45,688
In the Quest Log it's done,

86
00:04:46,138 --> 00:04:50,077
and the hundred credits on its Reward line are paid to the crew's side.

87
00:04:51,877 --> 00:04:55,491
Now add a second quest, one that finishes on time,

88
00:04:55,941 --> 00:04:57,887
with Done when, two minutes.

89
00:04:58,787 --> 00:05:00,425
Give it a briefing of its own,

90
00:05:00,875 --> 00:05:04,622
at least two paragraphs: what to do, and why it matters.

91
00:05:05,522 --> 00:05:07,695
That's just a number and a unit.

92
00:05:09,495 --> 00:05:11,732
There are five verbs built in,

93
00:05:12,182 --> 00:05:13,659
and they're all on the page.

94
00:05:15,459 --> 00:05:17,606
Next time we'll join quests together,

95
00:05:18,056 --> 00:05:19,608
so that one leads to the next.
